# Azure AI Vision Face Liveness Detection Web SDK is a gated package (Face Recognition
# Limited Access). It is not published to the public npm registry, so installs for these
# two scopes are routed to the private Azure DevOps feed instead.
#
# @azure/ai-vision-face-ui is intentionally NOT listed in package.json — the app loads it
# via a runtime dynamic import() and treats it as optional (see vite.config.ts's `external`
# check and GuidedDocumentCapture's try/catch), so plain `npm ci`/`npm install` never needs
# to resolve it and CI never needs AZURE_FACE_NPM_TOKEN. Declaring it as a real dependency
# previously broke `npm ci` everywhere with E401, since npm still hard-fails on a genuine
# auth error even for optionalDependencies.
#
# To enable real face-liveness detection locally:
# 1. Generate a Personal Access Token (scope: Packaging > Read) in the "msface" Azure
#    DevOps org, "SDK" project, "AzureAIVision" feed. Your org must already be approved
#    for Face Recognition Limited Access (https://aka.ms/facerecognition).
# 2. Export it and install the package explicitly (this updates your local
#    package.json/package-lock.json — do not commit that change unless every
#    contributor and CI runner will have the token):
#      export AZURE_FACE_NPM_TOKEN=<your-PAT>
#      npm install @azure/ai-vision-face-ui@^1.4.5 --save-optional
# Never commit the token itself — only the ${AZURE_FACE_NPM_TOKEN} reference below.
@azure:registry=https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/msface/SDK/_packaging/AzureAIVision/npm/registry/
@azure-ai-vision-face:registry=https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/msface/SDK/_packaging/AzureAIVision/npm/registry/
//pkgs.dev.azure.com/msface/SDK/_packaging/AzureAIVision/npm/registry/:_authToken=${AZURE_FACE_NPM_TOKEN}
